---
alwaysApply: true
---
Use Prisma ORM for type-safe queries and migration management.

OR use pg with sql-template-strings for raw queries when Prisma isn’t suitable.

Define models with clear naming, relationships, constraints, and indexes.

Use database migrations to keep schema consistent (prisma migrate, sqitch, etc.).

Keep SQL logic out of routes/controllers — move to services or repositories.

Never expose raw queries or sensitive fields (e.g., passwords, tokens) in APIs.

Prefer UUIDs or cuid() as primary keys when applicable.

Always hash sensitive data (e.g., bcrypt for passwords).

Seed initial data with care using dedicated scripts (prisma db seed, etc.).

Regularly back up the database and monitor performance (index slow queries).